260
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,160
I love you so much.

261
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,680
Oh, crap, don't wake up...

262
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:17,720
Where are Bill and Colleen?

263
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:19,720
They are in the kitchen, getting something to eat.

264
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,400
Can you believe how nice they are?

265
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,440
We have to leave.

266
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,480
Why? What did you do in the bathroom?

267
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,000
I didn't get to the bathroom.

268
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:30,360
I bumped into Owen on the way.

269
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:31,940
He didn't know he was adopted.

270
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:34,580
There's a slight chance l may have told him.

271
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,700
Oh, my God, where's my purse?

272
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,600
No, I can replace everything in there.

273
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,360
- Get that binder and let's go!  - Hi.

274
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,820
Some little snacks for everybody.

275
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:46,860
You don't have to eat the sour worms. Those are for Owen.

276
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:49,080
I'll go get him in a second.

277
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:52,440
By the way, you should know, we haven't told him he's adopted yet.

278
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,900
But kids are so intuitive.

279
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,960
Don't you think, on some level, he already knows?

280
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,960
- I'm adopted?  - See? Intuitive.

281
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:03,980
What? Where did you hear that?

282
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,540
He told me.

283
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:09,860
And he paid me 50 dollars not to tell.

284
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,460
Which, technically, now you should give back.

285
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,760
You told him he's adopted?

286
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:19,880
I'm sorry.

287
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,820
But You should have a sign out there or something.

288
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:24,860
Or at least whisper it to people when they come in the door.

289
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:28,700
"Owen doesn't know he's adopted, and he also thinks Santa is real."

290
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,020
He isn't?

291
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,740
We have to get out of here, baby.

292
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:43,720
Everyone, I would like to make a toast to Rachel and Joey.

293
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:48,700
And to love.

294
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:53,160
Ah, love!

295
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,980
L-O-V-E. Love.

296
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,720
L is for "life."

297
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,100
And what is life without love?

298
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,200
Oh, my God, are we supposed to answer?

299
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:11,020
O is for...

300
00:17:12,526 --> 00:17:13,907
"Oh, wow!"

301
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:28,560
The V is for this very surprising turn of events which I am still fine with, by the way.

302
00:17:30,405 --> 00:17:46,349
E is for how extremely normal I find it that you two are together.

303
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:56,460
And that one day you might get married and have children of your own.

304
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:03,220
- Dude, are you okay? - Totally.

305
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,440
Ross, you don't seem okay.

306
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:10,000
I'm sorry, it must be the pressure of entertaining.

307
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,440
I think everyone would feel better if we had some flan.

308
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:22,220
Wait, Ross. Ross, l--I have to take off.

309
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:24,100
- No!  - I'm sorry.

310
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,900
I have an early class in the morning.

311
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:29,600
But this has been lovely.

312
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:35,580
Wasn't it? And you thought it would be awkward with Joey.

313
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:37,760
And that you never really liked Rachel.

314
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:40,320
You are on fire!

315
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,520
I'll call you in the morning, okay?

316
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,480
- Okay. - All right.

317
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:50,540
God, Rachel, what Ross just said, that's just--

318
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,480
That's okay. Girls tend not to like me.

319
00:18:53,902 --> 00:18:55,292
Fine.

320
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:01,280
Okay. I guess it's just flan for three.

321
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:04,580
Hey, that rhymes.

322
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:11,040
You know what, Ross, I think we're gonna take off too.

323
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:15,340
Of course. God, I'm so stupid.

324
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,660
You guys are a couple now.

325
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,120
I mean, you probably just want to be alone.

326
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,780
No, it's just getting late--

327
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:24,480
It's fine. It's totally fine.

328
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,780
I've got plenty of margaritas. It's all good.

329
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,440
I don't even know what that's for.

330
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:42,620
You know what?

331
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:46,460
I think I'm gonna stay here and make sure he's okay.

332
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,960
That's probably a good idea.

333
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:49,360
I'll see you in the morning.

334
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:50,680
Okay.

335
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,820
Yeah, you know, Joey, l--

336
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:56,700
I don't think he's ever gonna be okay with this.

337
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,820
It doesn't look good, does it?

338
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:20,880
Morning.

339
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:23,480
- Here you go.  - Thanks.

340
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:28,320
- Did you stay here all night?  - Yeah.

341
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,480
So you took off my pants and shoes?

342
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:34,400
No...

343
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:38,620
You actually did that when you  were dancing to the <i>Chicago</i> soundtrack.

344
00:20:41,388 --> 00:20:45,980
Look, Ross about Rachel and l.

345
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:49,740
Listen, you don't have to worry about that because nothing's gonna happen.

346
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,740
What do you mean?

347
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:58,500
She and I said from the beginning we weren't gonna do anything unless you were okay with it.

348
00:20:58,516 --> 00:21:00,006
And clearly--

349
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:02,180
What are you talking about? I'm fine.

350
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:07,360
It's okay, Ross. You know, I totally understand.

351
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:09,440
Of course you're not fine. You're...

352
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,480
You're Ross and Rachel.

353
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,200
Yeah, except we're not.

354
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:25,700
I mean, we haven't been a couple in, like six years.

355
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,040
My God, is that right?

356
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:32,800
Has it been that long?

357
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:34,920
That's what I hear, yeah.

358
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:43,780
This is crazy.I mean, six years and because of me, you guys aren't gonna be together?

359
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,120
Can I ask you something?

360
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:53,160
Really what is this thing with you and Rachel?

361
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:58,000
Come on, you know me. You know...

362
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:01,260
Joey.

363
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:10,200
I'm crazy about her.

364
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:17,260
And she feels the same way?

365
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:21,120
I think so.

366
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:28,620
Well, then maybe it's time we all moved on.

367
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:32,060
Yeah, but, Ross, I mean, you're not okay with it, so--

368
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:35,200
No, but I want to be.

369
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:38,600
I will be.

370
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:44,260
Besides, I'm with Charlie, right?

371
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:47,880
Oh, my God, I'm still with Charlie, aren't l?

372
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,460
- She didn't see the dance, did she?  - No...

373
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:54,260
No, that was--That was just for me.

374
00:22:58,940 --> 00:22:59,580
Hey, you...?

375
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,020
You sure about this?

376
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,420
Yeah, I'm sure.

377
00:23:08,061 --> 00:23:12,002
And we're okay?

378
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:25,100
- Hey, Pheebs. - Hey.

379
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:27,360
We just want to give you a heads up.

380
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:29,780
- Bill and Colleen hate us.  - Why?

381
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:32,360
Owen didn't know he's adopted and Monica told him.

382
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,350
What?

383
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:35,800
Still, he had to find out sometime.

384
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:39,380
How would you like it if someone told the triplets that you gave birth to them?

385
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:46,480
I'm gonna go tell Emma she was an accident.

